---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';

const title = `Projects — ${SITE_TITLE}`;
const description = 'Selected work in Linux distribution engineering, KDE, Kubuntu, Snapcraft, and open-source infrastructure.';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description || SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
    <style>
      .grid-bg { position: fixed; inset: 0; background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(55,138,221,.04) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(55,138,221,.04) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 40px 40px; pointer-events: none; z-index: 0; }
      .orb { position: fixed; width: 600px; height: 600px; border-radius: 50%; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(24,95,165,.15) 0%, transparent 70%); top: -200px; right: -200px; pointer-events: none; z-index: 0; }
      main { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 760px; width: calc(100% - 4rem); margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 0; }
      .page-tag { font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
      h1 { font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--text); }
      .intro { max-width: 620px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
      .project-list { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
      .project { background: var(--bg2); border: 1px solid var(--blue-border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.5rem; }
      .project h2 { font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; font-size: 15px; color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
      .project p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
      .project .status { font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--text-dim); text-transform: uppercase; }
      .project a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--blue-border); }
      .project a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }
      @media (max-width: 600px) { main { width: calc(100% - 2rem); padding: 2.5rem 0; } }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="grid-bg"></div>
    <div class="orb"></div>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <div class="page-tag">// selected work</div>
      <h1>Projects &amp; engineering</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        A selection of the ecosystems, tools, and infrastructure I've worked on.
        Much of this work happens in collaboration with upstream developers and
        volunteer communities; these notes highlight the engineering problems and
        the solutions, not just the project names.
      </p>
      <div class="project-list">
        <article class="project">
          <h2>KDE Snaps &amp; shared runtimes</h2>
          <p>
            I helped bring the Snap model to KDE applications after Canonical introduced
            the technology, and have been involved with KDE Snaps from the early days —
            serving as their solo maintainer for much of the project's existence. The work
            spans application packaging, shared KDE content snaps and runtimes, Qt/KF
            integration, and the ongoing maintenance that keeps the ecosystem usable.
          </p>
          <p>
            My current engineering focus includes the KDE Neon Snapcraft extension,
            Core26 support, launcher and environment integration, and GPU compatibility
            across Snap base generations.
          </p>
          <div class="status">KDE · Snapcraft · Qt6 · KF6 · Core26 · Ongoing</div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <h2>KDE Neon Core</h2>
          <p>
            I developed the business plan for KDE Neon Core: a complete operating-system
            initiative built on Ubuntu Core, not the existing KDE neon desktop distribution.{" "}
            <a href="https://www.enioka.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">enioka</a>{" "}
            took up the proposal and brought the work forward for Core24, then invited me
            back to contribute to the Core26 effort.
          </p>
          <div class="status">KDE · Ubuntu Core · Product planning · Core24 / Core26</div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <h2>KDE continuous integration</h2>
          <p>
            During Season of KDE, I built the first iteration of KDE's continuous
            integration infrastructure, hosted at <code>build.kde.org</code> and powered
            by Jenkins. That work helped establish automated build infrastructure for
            KDE's development ecosystem and became a turning point in my engineering career.
          </p>
          <div class="status">KDE · Jenkins · CI/CD · Foundational work</div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <h2>KDE neon — original team</h2>
          <p>
            I was a significant part of the original team that brought KDE neon to life:
            a new way of delivering the latest KDE software on a stable Ubuntu LTS base,
            with CI-driven builds and integration at its heart. This grew out of the
            close collaboration and experience of the early Kubuntu team, and became
            one of the defining projects of that chapter of my career.
          </p>
          <div class="status">KDE · Ubuntu LTS · CI-driven distribution · Original team</div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <h2>Kubuntu &amp; Ubuntu packaging</h2>
          <p>
            I joined Kubuntu in 2012 and began my packaging work during the transition
            from monolithic <code>kdelibs</code> to modular KDE Frameworks, helping package
            the effort for Kubuntu and integrate it into Ubuntu. I later returned for the
            Noble release and contributed to the Resolute LTS release and early work on the{" "}
            <a href="https://www.einpresswire.com/article/930823977/kubuntu-focus-techpaladin-software-and-kde-e-v-announce-the-bullet-proof-kde-software-initiative" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bulletproof KDE software initiative</a>{" "}
            through Kubuntu Focus. That work has since moved to Techpaladin,
            whose team I wish well.
          </p>
          <div class="status">Kubuntu Developer · Kubuntu Council · Ubuntu · Packaging</div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <h2>Reproducible builds</h2>
          <p>
            Through an early Outreach program, I was hired by the Linux Foundation to
            contribute to the early reproducible builds effort. I worked on making
            software packages reproducible, including CMake, helping improve the ability
            to independently verify that builds can be recreated from their source.
          </p>
          <div class="status">Linux Foundation · Reproducible Builds · Packaging</div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <h2>DCI &amp; Netrunner</h2>
          <p>
            After my KDE CI work, I joined Blue Systems to maintain DCI, a Debian-based
            continuous integration system that underpinned the Netrunner distribution.
            This brought together my experience in Debian, build automation, and the
            practical engineering of a Linux distribution.
          </p>
          <div class="status">Blue Systems · Debian · CI/CD · Netrunner</div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <h2>Debian packaging &amp; Python</h2>
          <p>
            My Debian work has included contributions with the Debian KDE/Qt team,
            Python packaging work with Mycroft, and earlier reproducible-builds
            contributions. I am an official Debian Developer with upload privileges.
            My Debian activity is quieter while I balance other commitments, but it
            remains an important part of my open-source work.
          </p>
          <div class="status">Debian Developer · KDE/Qt · Python · Packaging</div>
        </article>

        <article class="project">
          <h2>Open-source community service</h2>
          <p>
            Alongside engineering, I served for two years on the Ubuntu Community Council,
            contributing to community governance. I am also a member of the Kubuntu Council,
            supporting the project and its community.
          </p>
          <div class="status">Ubuntu Community Council · Kubuntu Council · Community</div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
